        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>What do Bowflex T9 treadmill reviews say?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Independent reviews agree it is a sturdy, quiet folding treadmill with a 22 by 60-inch deck, a generous 15% incline and easy dial controls. The two consistent complaints are that Bluetooth cannot connect a heart-rate strap and an app at the same time, and that the cushioning is firmer than some prefer. We have not tested it.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the Bowflex T9 a good treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On its published figures, yes, particularly for runners and heavier users: 22 by 60 inches, 0 to 15% incline, 12 mph, a 350 lb rating, and lifetime frame and motor cover with three years on parts. Its 3.5 HP is a test-setting rating rather than a continuous-duty figure, and labour cover is one year.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Bowflex T9 vs T6: which should I buy?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Both have 15% incline, 12 mph and lifetime frame and motor cover. The T9 adds a 22-inch-wide deck instead of 20, a 350 lb rating instead of 325, a higher motor rating on Bowflex’s test basis and a colour console. Tall or broad runners and heavier users benefit most; walkers rarely need it.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does the Bowflex T9 need a JRNY subscription?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. The T9 works fully without any subscription. It connects over Bluetooth to JRNY, Peloton and Zwift if you want app content, but each is a separate paid subscription, so check the current price of the one you want.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does the Bowflex T9 fold?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes, but not flat. Bowflex lists it at 77.2 inches long assembled and 48.6 inches long folded, staying 37 inches wide and 67.6 inches tall. It weighs 282 lb and rolls on two transport wheels. Check ceiling height too: Bowflex recommends the user’s height plus 20.75 inches.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the weight limit on the Bowflex T9?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Bowflex lists a maximum user weight of 350 lb, and independent reviews give the same figure. That is 25 lb more than the T6.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

